{{- else if eq .Category "perf" }}
## How the Performance & Web Vitals Analysis Pipeline Works

The `perf` engine audits component code for Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP) and client-side hydration efficiency:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Inputs ["1. Workspace Inputs"]
        Components["Component Files (*.astro, *.tsx)"]
    end

    subgraph Inspection ["2. Asset & Script Inspection"]
        Components --> AST["Leaf IR Traversal"]
        AST --> Images["Media Elements (img, video, picture)"]
        AST --> Scripts["Script & Hydration Boundaries"]
    end

    subgraph Evaluation ["3. Core Web Vitals Evaluation"]
        Images --> LCP["LCP Optimizer (fetchpriority='high', anti-lazy hero)"]
        Images --> CLS["CLS Preventer (explicit width/height & aspect-ratio)"]
        Scripts --> INP["INP Guard (render-blocking scripts & thread delays)"]
    end

    subgraph Output ["4. Results"]
        LCP --> Decision{"CWV Compliance Check"}
        CLS --> Decision
        INP --> Decision
        Decision -- "Compliant" --> Safe["Pass"]
        Decision -- "Violation" --> Diag["Diagnostic: perf.*"]
    end
```

### Pipeline Flow:
1. **LCP Optimization:** Ensures above-the-fold hero images use `fetchpriority="high"` and do not specify `loading="lazy"`.
2. **CLS Shift Prevention:** Requires explicit `width` and `height` attributes or CSS `aspect-ratio` on all visual media elements.
3. **INP & Thread Guard:** Detects synchronous scripts and un-deferred client islands that delay the main thread.

